# Goals — folder structure
# Goals are now split by domain. Copy the examples below into data/goals/<domain>.md
# The entire data/goals/ folder is gitignored — your data stays local.

# ── data/goals/workout.md ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Workout Goals

## Runner Profile
- Current max distance: X km
- Current pace: X:XX/km
- Runs per week: N
- Other activities: [e.g. strength, cycling, bouldering]

## Race Goal
- Event: [race name]
- Date: [YYYY-MM-DD]
- Target finish: [time] (~X:XX/km pace)
- Strategy: [your strategy]

## Training Plan
- Schedule: N runs/week
  - Short run: X–Y km (midweek)
  - Long run: build from X km → Y km (weekends)


# ── data/goals/growth.md ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Growth Goals

## Personal Growth Goal
- Goal: [e.g. build a stronger personal voice]
- Noticed in: [where the pattern shows up]
- Underlying fear / root cause: [honest reflection]
- Status: [in progress / parked / done]


# ── data/goals/lifestyle.md ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Lifestyle Goals

## [Habit name]
- Goal: [specific target, e.g. ≤2.5 hrs screen time/day]
- Baseline: [current level]
- Why: [reason]
- Exception: [any exceptions]


# ── data/goals/career.md ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Career Goals

## [Goal name]
- Goal: [specific outcome]
- Timeline: [date or milestone]
- Current status: [where you are now]


# ── data/goals/dutch.md ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dutch Language Goals

## Dutch Language Goal
- Goal: Reach [level] Dutch proficiency
- Target date: [date]
- Current level: [e.g. A2]
- Strategy: [how you plan to get there]
